@ev_fiesta
title: La fiesta del santo
new-page: true
face-image: img/elpueblo.jpg
subtitle: The column is invited to the village's patron day
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and apoyo_popular >= 40 and time >= f_ev_last + 3
priority: 2
frequency: 45
max-visits: 4
on-arrival: f_ev_last = time

= La fiesta del santo

The village is holding its patron saint's feast, and it sends word up the mountain that the compañeros are welcome. It is an enormous compliment and an enormous risk: half the state's informers work fiestas, the army knows the calendar as well as you do, and a column that comes down for a dance can be a column that gets surrounded at a dance.

- @fie_bajar: Go — a few of you, unarmed, as neighbours. *(+apoyo, +moral; a real risk)*
- @fie_mandar: Send a token: a message read aloud, and a contribution for the band and the fireworks. *(small +apoyo, no risk)*
- @fie_prohibir: Forbid it and keep everyone in camp. *(safe; the column resents it, the village notices)*

@fie_bajar
on-arrival: {! var _r=Math.random()*100; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(6,_h*0.35); Q.f_moral+=8; if(_r < (Q.f_cerco||0)*0.6){ Q.f_cerco+=18; Q.f_hombres-=1; Q.f_bajas+=1; } !}

They go down in clean shirts with no rifles and they dance, and for one night they are not a guerrilla but somebody's cousins home from the mountain. It does more for the column's soul than any victory, and it does something for the village too: these are *our* boys, not strangers with guns. [? if f_cerco >= 55 : Somebody at the edge of the plaza was counting faces, though, and the patrols on the road double within the week. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

@fie_mandar
on-arrival: {! Q.apoyo_popular+=2; Q.f_moral+=2; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)-2; if(Q.funds<0){Q.funds=0;} !}

A courier carries down a short message to be read between the mass and the dancing, and enough money for the band's mezcal. It is correct, and prudent, and everyone understands the reason. It is also a letter where a face was wanted.

- @root: Continuar.

@fie_prohibir
on-arrival: {! Q.f_moral-=6; Q.apoyo_popular-=3; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+2; Q.f_cerco-=4; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} !}

No one goes. The discipline is correct and the men hate it, and two of them lie awake doing the arithmetic of what they have given up — the fiesta, the girl, the ordinary life happening four kilometres downhill without them. This is how armies of volunteers quietly begin to leak.

- @root: Continuar.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@ev_maestro
title: El maestro rural
new-page: true
face-image: img/maestros.jpg
subtitle: The schoolteacher — Guerrero's oldest revolutionary profession
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and time >= f_ev_last + 3
priority: 4
frequency: 45
max-visits: 3
on-arrival: f_ev_last = time

= El maestro rural

He walks into camp with chalk dust still on his sleeve — a normalista from Ayotzinapa, twenty-four, teaching in a two-room school three valleys over, and he wants to know whether the movement has any use for him. In Guerrero this is not an unusual conversation: Lucio was a teacher, Genaro was a teacher, and the rural normal schools have been producing more revolutionaries than the state's own agrarian grievances for forty years. He can organize, he can write, and everyone in six villages already trusts him.

- @mae_cuadro: Take him into the column as a cadre — a political officer who can teach the recruits to read and to argue. *(+discipline, +legend)*
- @mae_dejarlo: Leave him where he is, and make him the movement's eyes and voice in six villages. *(+apoyo, +intelligence — the network deepens)*

@mae_cuadro
on-arrival: {! Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+7; Q.f_moral+=4; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2; Q.f_hombres+=1; !}

He turns out to be worth three fighters, which is what teachers always are in this war: within a month the recruits are being taught why as well as how, the communiqués stop reading like a pamphlet translated from Russian, and the column argues about politics in the evenings instead of about food. Every serious guerrilla the Americas produced had one of him. Several were led by one.

- @root: Continuar.

@mae_dejarlo
on-arrival: {! var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(5,_h*0.3); Q.inteligencia+=5; Q.sup_teachers=(Q.sup_teachers||0)+3; Q.f_ev_last=Q.time; !}

You tell him the hardest thing a volunteer can hear: that he is worth more in his classroom than in your column. He is disappointed for about a week and then he becomes the most valuable thing the movement has in that district — a man every family trusts, who knows which boys are ready, which fathers can be asked, and which one of them has started talking to the sergeant.

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# LA VIDA INTERNA DE LA COLUMNA
# =====================================================================
@ev_mujeres
title: Las que llegaron a pelear
new-page: true
face-image: img/adelitas.jpg
subtitle: Women in the column, and the column's opinion about it
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_hombres >= 20 and time >= f_ev_last + 3
priority: 4
frequency: 45
max-visits: 2
on-arrival: f_ev_last = time

= Las que llegaron a pelear

Three women have come up the mountain and they have not come to cook. One is a normalista, one is the sister of a compañero the army took, one has simply walked eleven hours and will not explain herself further. Half the column assumes they will be given the kitchen and the wounded. The women assume otherwise, and say so. It is 1971 in rural Guerrero and this is a genuine argument, and how you settle it will be quoted back at you for the rest of the war.

- @muj_combate: They fight. Same training, same watch, same rifle — and the men who object can take it up with the enemy. *(+fighters, +legend; friction now)*
- @muj_apoyo: Put them in the support structure — couriers, safe houses, the network. *(+intelligence, +apoyo; a compromise nobody loves)*

@muj_combate
on-arrival: {! Q.f_hombres+=3; Q.f_moral-=2; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+2; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2; Q.feminismo=(Q.feminismo||0)+8; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(3,_h*0.2); !}

You settle it in one sentence in front of everybody and the grumbling lasts about a month, until the first serious contact, after which nobody mentions it again. What it does to the villages is more interesting than what it does to the column: mothers who would not have let a son go start sending word that their daughter is asking. A movement that arms women is telling the sierra something about what it intends to build, and the sierra hears it.

- @root: Continuar.

@muj_apoyo
on-arrival: {! Q.inteligencia+=4; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(4,_h*0.25); Q.feminismo=(Q.feminismo||0)+3; !}

They become the nervous system of the whole zone — carrying messages through checkpoints no armed man could pass, renting the houses, moving the medicine, knowing everything. It is indispensable work and it is, everyone quietly understands, the work that gets least written down. One of them says so, once, and does not say it again.

- @root: Continuar.

